==German==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=de}}
[[Image:Breads.jpg|thumb|Zwei '''Brote''' — Two '''loaves of bread''' (2)]]
[[Image:Rye bread.JPG|thumb|Mehrere Scheiben Roggen'''brot''' — Several slices of rye '''bread''' (1)]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|brōt}}, from {{inh|de|goh|brōt}} (attested since the 8th century), from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*braudą}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*bʰrew-||to seethe, to boil}}. Originally, the meaning of ''Brot'' was ''"what has been fermented, leaven"'' and may be a nominal derivative from {{cog|gem-pro|*brewwaną||to brew}} (whence German {{m|de|brauen}}). It replaced the older {{m|de|Laib||loaf}} which was the more common term in Old High German (compare the use of {{m|ang|hlāf}} and {{m|ang|brēad}} in Old English).<ref>Pfeifer, Wolfgang. 1995, 2005. ''Etymologisches Wörterbuch des Deutschen.'' München: dtv. {{ISBN|3423325119}}.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bʁoːt/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Brot.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Brot.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|oːt|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|Brot|lang=de}}

